Touchpad gestures: switch windows with three fingers, desktops with four, the way the fingers go.

KWin switches virtual desktops with both three- and four-finger sideways swipes, and the desktops
move like a sheet being dragged: swiping left goes to the desktop on the right. Change it to:
- Three fingers switch windows, as on Windows (TouchpadGestures, at the end of tabbox.cpp): a
  sideways swipe opens Alt+Tab's switcher on the previous window, moving the fingers on moves the
  selection along (sideways one window per step, within its row, and up or down one row), stopping
  at the edges, and lifting them switches to it. A quick flick switches to the previous window
  without showing the switcher. A swipe that starts up or down is left to KWin.
- Desktops move the way the fingers go, as when scrolling: swiping left goes to the desktop on the
  left (VirtualDesktopManager::initShortcuts()). Touchscreen swipes are left alone.

The settings, in kwinrc's [TouchpadGestures] (System Settings > Danylo's Linux Tweaks > Touchpad
Gestures), apply when KWin reloads its settings (qdbus6 org.kde.KWin /KWin reconfigure):
  ThreeFingerSwipe=Windows      (Desktops: KWin's, None: nothing)
  DesktopsFollowFingers=true    (false: KWin's direction)
  OpenDistance=2.5              (mm sideways before the switcher opens)
  StepDistance=5                (mm further for each next window)
  SwitchRows=true
  RowDistance=5                 (mm up or down for each next row)
  AxisDistance=0.5              (mm: the movement counts in pieces this long, each along the axis
                                it mostly went, and the fingers go this far past a step or row's
                                edge to change it, so that drift and jitter don't)
  FlickTime=90                  (ms before the switcher shows: a swipe over before is a flick)
Out-of-range values give the defaults above.

Made to keep applying to new KWin versions: the window switching uses only TabBox's public
functions (and finds the rows from the switcher's Qt Quick GridView) and is added at the end of
tabbox.cpp, with one call at the end of initShortcuts(); the desktop hunk replaces just the four
touchpad swipe registrations, unchanged since KWin 6.6.

Applied by scripts/patches/patch-library, see scripts/configure_hardware.

